      "writtenOn": "2026-02-13T16:09:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Even if we forget that we touch `arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/pkvm.c` as well, not just `arch/x86/kvm/x86.c`, this is still purely pKVM hypervisor-specific change: it doesn\u0027t affect behavior or compilation of host KVM code, it only affects pKVM hypervisor code (as x86.c is reused by the hypervisor code)?\n\nI think we have a lot of precedents of patches that have `pKVM: x86:` or `pKVM: VMX:` even though they touch original KVM files only, since changes they make are for the pKVM hypervisor, not for the host.",
      "parentUuid": "eb14ce5f_9dd04998",
